import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 659 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 660 | 2026-10-25 | **Four notes from her 23:10-23:15 review, one build (V).** Built on row 659. (1) 'The King and Queen home animation, here': the staff chapter's clef pictures (The Queen's five, The King's five) come alive on screen (SfClefHome): the chess piece leaves its place beside the '=', walks onto its line and goes home, the Queen along the G line and round the curl, the King along the F line past his two guards (the dots); the line lights, its note sounds, a soft coral ring marks home. Print keeps the still picture. (2) 'Show high C and low C too, so the mirror is felt': Line and space names' fold (screen, tool and page 5) now folds high C onto low C as well, two ladders out; page 5's text says so. (3) 'Loud & soft comes too late, before the staff; Pitch can sit apart, in an attic': the Beginner floor is now Posture, Patterns, Beat, Alphabet, Hand positions, (Listen and sing), Note values, Loud & soft, The staff, Steps & skips, Line and space names, Time signatures, Tones; Loud & soft's tunes (right hand, C position) carry finger numbers over the notes so they can be played before the staff is read, and its tie is met there first (no chapter cross-reference). Pitch, Hz & range moves to a new top storey, the Attic ('rooms to explore any time'); the house says 'four floors and an attic'. (4) 'A selector to see just the rhythm rooms': topic chips above the house (All, Pitch, Rhythm, Touch and expression, Technique, Pieces, Beside the five, each with its count) keep that topic's rooms clear and pale the rest; the choice is remembered on the device. Whether the Home is still needed: hers to decide after trying the chips. Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/patch684.py, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/v684.jsx. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
